      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "> With a large `-bytespersigop`, its sigop-adjusted weight does not fit in the `int32_t`\r\n\r\nNot sure this is a valid use-case, but the parsing is likely broken in this case anyway on this pull and master: It is parsed as i64, then assigned to u32, then used in a i32 calculation. Every step either truncates, wraps, or aborts. I'd say if this is fixed, it would be good to fix all of them.",
