      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree fb1d34a2f7ed74b083d4139d3a28b22009ee274f\nparent 649bc0a645eb127a9b1e6d078f8d129be6380c87\nauthor Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792074980 +0200\ncommitter Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792083799 +0200\n\ninit: refuse -bytespersigop values that overflow\n\n-bytespersigop is parsed as int64_t and stored in an unsigned int, so\na negative value wraps and a value of 2^32 or more is truncated: -1\nbecomes 4294967295, and 4294967296 becomes 0, which silently turns off\nthe sigop adjustment.\n\nThe stored value is then multiplied by the sigop cost of a transaction\ninto sigop-adjusted sizes, and these are narrowed to int32_t: the weight\nused by TxGraph, and the total vsize of a package in CheckFeeRate. A\nstandard transaction has a sigop cost of at most\nMAX_STANDARD_TX_SIGOPS_COST (16000), so its vsize is at most\n16000 * bytespersigop / WITNESS_SCALE_FACTOR (4), and a package holds at\nmost MAX_PACKAGE_COUNT (25) transactions. The package total fits in\nint32_t while 25 * 4000 * bytespersigop <= INT32_MAX (2147483647), that\nis up to 21474: 100000 * 21474 = 2147400000, while\n100000 * 21475 = 2147500000 does not fit. Above that, a package of 25\ntransactions at the limit aborts a debug build on\nAssume(virtual_bytes >= 0) in CFeeRate::GetFee; above 134217, so does a\nsingle transaction, on Assume(feerate.size > 0) in\nTxGraphImpl::AddTransaction.\n\nRefuse at startup any value outside [0, 21474], before it is stored.\n",
