      "updated_at": "2026-10-15T21:14:12Z",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "Agreed, fixed in 7d37a758b3: `-bytespersigop` outside [0, 21474] is now refused at startup, so it is stored without wrapping or truncation. 21474 is the largest value at which a package of 25 transactions at the standard sigops limit keeps an int32 size. A bound of 134217 would cover one transaction, but a package of 5 then aborts a debug build. I kept the sigops check before staging as a second commit, because a single transaction far over the limit still overflows at 21474.\n",
